{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_0","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc 'cat /Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-14-use-acceptance/d375-measure/packet-v7-2.md'","aggregated_output":"# Packet v7-2\n\n**The question:** How much will the five largest AI hyperscalers spend on data centers in calendar 2026?\n\nDue 2027-04-30. Possible answers:\n- 1 Below $700 billion: Combined spending is less than $700 billion.\n- 2 $700 billion to below $775 billion: Combined spending is at least $700 billion and less than $775 billion.\n- 3 $775 billion to below $825 billion: Combined spending is at least $775 billion and less than $825 billion; this is the neutral comparison range around the author's nearly $800 billion estimate.\n- 4 $825 billion to below $900 billion: Combined spending is at least $825 billion and less than $900 billion.\n- 5 $900 billion or more: Combined spending is at least $900 billion.\n\n**7 statements read on 2026-09-23:**\n\n- **v7-2-1** (stored attribution: AMD): AMD reported Q2 FY2026 Data Center revenue growth of 107%.\n  - Passage: \"Advanced Micro Devices ( NASDAQ:AMD ) posted Q2 fiscal 2026 revenue of $11.536 billion, up 50.11%, with Data Center up 107%.\"\n- **v7-2-2** (stored attribution: NVIDIA): NVIDIA had helped arrange over $500 billion of third-party capital with six infrastructure providers.\n  - Passage: \"helped arrange over $500 billion of third-party capital with six infrastructure providers.\"\n- **v7-2-3** (stored attribution: Alibaba's chip unit): Alibaba's chip unit unveiled its Zhenwu V900 AI chip, which it said triples its predecessor's performance, and plans to put it on sale in early 2027.\n  - Passage: \"At the Apsara Conference in Hangzhou on Tuesday, Alibaba's chip unit unveiled the Zhenwu V900 chip , which triples the performance of its predecessor and will go on sale in early 2027.\"\n- **v7-2-4** (stored attribution: 24/7 Wall St. author): The 24/7 Wall St. author forecast NVIDIA gross margin of 71% to 72% in Q4 FY2027 and 72% to 73% in FY2028.\n  - Passage: \"Gross margins are expected to bottom in the 71% to 72% range in Q4 on memory cost inflation, recovering to 72% to 73% in fiscal 2028 as volumes scale.\"\n- **v7-2-5** (stored attribution: 24/7 Wall St. author): The 24/7 Wall St. author forecast hyperscaler capital spending of nearly $800 billion in calendar 2026 and $1.3 trillion in calendar 2027.\n  - Passage: \"Hyperscaler capex is expected to reach nearly 800 billion in 2026 and 1.3 trillion in 2027, a wave that also pulls in the power, cooling, and networking suppliers we profiled in a free report on seven AI infrastructure names that aren't chipmakers.\"\n- **v7-2-6** (stored attribution: Nvidia and Amazon): Nvidia and Amazon reached a recent deal involving 2 million GPUs.\n  - Passage: \"The recent deal with Amazon (AMZN) involving 2 million GPUs\"\n- **v7-2-7** (stored attribution: Lisa Su, AMD CEO): AMD CEO Lisa Su said customer demand for AMD's Helios AI systems was very strong and tracking ahead of the company's initial forecast.\n  - Passage: \"customer pull for the company's new Helios AI systems is \"very strong and tracking ahead of our initial forecast,\"\"\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_1","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"item\":\"v7-2-1\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"AMD's revenue growth does not give hyperscaler data center spending.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v7-2-2\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The third-party capital is not identified as 2026 spending by the five hyperscalers.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v7-2-3\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The chip launch and 2027 sale plan do not establish 2026 data center spending.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v7-2-4\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"NVIDIA's forecast gross margins do not give hyperscaler spending.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v7-2-5\",\"bears\":\"yes\",\"why\":\"It forecasts nearly $800 billion in hyperscaler capital spending in calendar 2026.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v7-2-6\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"The GPU deal gives no spending amount or 2026 delivery schedule.\"}\n{\"item\":\"v7-2-7\",\"bears\":\"no\",\"why\":\"Demand for AMD's systems does not specify hyperscaler spending in 2026.\"}\n{\"done\":true,\"items\":7}"}}
